 234:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c **** /**
 235:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c ****  * Search the ARP table for a matching or new entry.
 236:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c ****  *
 237:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c ****  * If an IP address is given, return a pending or stable ARP entry that matches
 238:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c ****  * the address. If no match is found, create a new entry with this address set,
 239:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c ****  * but in state ETHARP_EMPTY. The caller must check and possibly change the
 240:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c ****  * state of the returned entry.
 241:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c ****  *
 242:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c ****  * If ipaddr is NULL, return a initialized new entry in state ETHARP_EMPTY.
 243:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c ****  *
 244:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c ****  * In all cases, attempt to create new entries from an empty entry. If no
 245:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c ****  * empty entries are available and ETHARP_FLAG_TRY_HARD flag is set, recycle
 246:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c ****  * old entries. Heuristic choose the least important entry for recycling.
 247:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c ****  *
 248:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c ****  * @param ipaddr IP address to find in ARP cache, or to add if not found.
 249:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c ****  * @param flags See @ref etharp_state
 250:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c ****  * @param netif netif related to this address (used for NETIF_HWADDRHINT)
 251:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c ****  *
 252:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c ****  * @return The ARP entry index that matched or is created, ERR_MEM if no
