 899:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c **** /**
 900:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c ****  * Send an ARP request for the given IP address and/or queue a packet.
 901:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c ****  *
 902:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c ****  * If the IP address was not yet in the cache, a pending ARP cache entry
 903:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c ****  * is added and an ARP request is sent for the given address. The packet
 904:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c ****  * is queued on this entry.
 905:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c ****  *
 906:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c ****  * If the IP address was already pending in the cache, a new ARP request
 907:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c ****  * is sent for the given address. The packet is queued on this entry.
 908:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c ****  *
 909:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c ****  * If the IP address was already stable in the cache, and a packet is
 910:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c ****  * given, it is directly sent and no ARP request is sent out.
 911:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c ****  *
 912:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c ****  * If the IP address was already stable in the cache, and no packet is
 913:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c ****  * given, an ARP request is sent out.
 914:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c ****  *
 915:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/etharp.c ****  * @param netif The lwIP network interface on which ipaddr
